  "id": "read-update-sequence-dependent-bindings",
  "description": "Dependency normalization for @name references. A member whose creating member ended transiently is itself transient: it fails with idempotency-in-progress, retains nothing, and releases its claim, so a retry executes the creator and its dependent. An expired creator still binds its dependent: the tombstone keeps the allocated identity and kind, so the dependent's identity uses the resolved binding and its retained disposition answers unchanged. A permanently failed creator makes its dependent's binding permanently unavailable, and both retained failures answer a retry exactly as successes would. Conditions are narrated, not observed. Illustrative wire example; not evidence.",
